    <section class="lesson-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 · JULY 4, 1776</p>
      <h2>A declaration — not the end of the war</h2>
      <p>On July 4, 1776, the Continental Congress adopted the Declaration of Independence. The document announced that the thirteen colonies considered themselves free and independent states. It also presented arguments about natural rights and the authority of government.</p>
      <p>The Declaration did not end the Revolutionary War. Fighting continued until 1783, when the Treaty of Paris formally recognized American independence. The Declaration became one of the most influential statements of American political ideals, but it did not establish the detailed structure of the federal government.</p>
      <div class="document-panel">
        <span class="number">PRIMARY SOURCE · 1776</span>
        <h3>The Declaration of Independence</h3>
        <p>One of its best-known ideas is that legitimate government depends on the consent of the people it governs.</p>
        <p class="ru">Одна из важнейших идей документа — законная власть должна опираться на согласие народа, которым она управляет.</p>
